<div class="sec">
  <div class="sechead">
    <span class="k">Who it is for</span>
    <h2 class="h2">One person or a whole team.</h2>
    <p class="lead">The same install, whether it watches a side project or the systems your business depends on.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="aud">
    <div class="audc">
      <span class="audk m">Personal projects</span>
      <h3>Watch what you run at home.</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>One <code>docker compose</code>, one SQLite file, no account.</li>
        <li>Know when the NAS, the blog or the backup job quietly dies.</li>
        <li>A status page for the people who use your things.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="audc">
      <span class="audk m">Teams and businesses</span>
      <h3>Run it for the people who depend on you.</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Incidents with a timeline, a responder and acknowledgement.</li>
        <li>Alerts routed by rule to your team's webhook or email.</li>
        <li>A public status page on your own domain, with the history on your server.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
